  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-31T16:33:11.768Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The trust system provides some nice ranks, but the high ranks such as 'Trusted' don't mean a user is 'trusted' by any means, more that they've uploaded a lot of avatars/worlds and are known in the community.\nA lot of trusted users have horribly unoptimised avatars and full screen shaders on them, in what world does breaking most of VRChat's content guidelines make a user 'Trusted'?\nWould it not make more sense to have a Trusted rank for users that comply with peformance guidelines and create content that is 'trusted' to fit within the game's guidelines?\nI'm interested to see people's opinions on this though. :p\n\n(Totally aware a lot of people would be against this, as people are against the performance stats system, and where against the trust system. Do you really want sub 30-40FPS though? Some encouragement for user's to learn optimisation techniques would be great)",
